From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 17:17:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: wire Tier-1 NWeb methods

Wire the Tier-1 batch of NWeb controller methods to Servo, backed by new
nav-step, page-scroll and media-session bridge fns.

On-device coverage: ControllerPage in the test app exposes one button per
wired API, reporting `ArkWebTest: <name>=<value>` to hilog;
test_controller.py drives them via its invoke() helper and
test_throttle.py covers the render-throttle composition; since throttling
hides the WebView, it also checks that a page backgrounded and foregrounded
again paints and handles a tap. test_focus.py checks that a page in a newly
built WebView sees `document.hasFocus()`. ControllerPage's cookie buttons
let test_cookies.py check the cookie manager: cookies from `Set-Cookie` and
`document.cookie` are returned, and a cookie set from ArkTS reaches the
server on the next load. The history-nav test asserts a fresh title after
back/forward (relies on the URL-bar sync fix in the preceding commits).

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_controller.py, uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_throttle.py, uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_focus.py and uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_cookies.py on a device (after uv run ports/arkweb/tools/build_test_app.py).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; 2026-10-08 sync -- added test_focus.py, test_cookies.py with the ControllerPage cookie buttons, and repaint and tap checks after foregrounding to test_throttle.py, for upstream's focus, visibility and cookie changes)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
